# Monitor README maintenance

When a change under `HPCPerfStats/monitor/` affects **how developers build, test, or navigate the tree**, or **where major logic lives**, update documentation in the same change (or immediately after):

1. **`HPCPerfStats/monitor/README.md`** — landing page: package overview, directory layout, quick build and test, and the index of every page under `monitor/docs/`.
2. **`HPCPerfStats/monitor/docs/reference/source-modules.md`** — the key source modules table and per-collector behaviour, when modules are added, renamed, split, or removed.
3. **`HPCPerfStats/monitor/docs/how-to/*.md`** — build/RPM/fleet matrices (`build-the-rpm.md`), deploy order (`deploy-to-nodes.md`), correctness campaign and check inventory (`run-correctness-campaign.md`), profiling (`profile-the-daemon.md`), cross-compile (`cross-compile.md`).
4. **`HPCPerfStats/monitor/tests/README.md`** — when only the test suite layout, `Makefile.am` rules, or `run_tests.sh` behavior changes.

Do **not** duplicate the on-disk stats format in the README or the quadrant pages; it lives in **`docs/RAW_DATA_FORMAT.md`** (format + Python reader) and the generated **`docs/METRICS_REFERENCE.md`** (per-key meanings), kept current under **monitor-raw-data-format-docs**. The plain-text **`README`** only points there.

Typical triggers: new top-level dirs, moved tests, new `src/*.c` units called out in conventions, configure/Automake behavior visible to contributors, or consumer contract / listend expectations noted in the docs.

Also update when:

- **Two-tier** consumer rollout status or `enable_slow_tier` guidance changes (`docs/explanation/design.md`; **monitor-consumer-schema-migration**).
- **Breaking migrations** (IB merge, GPU schema, typename/device/key renames) — add a legacy vs current table to **`docs/reference/legacy-formats.md`**: decoding older archives is current consumer behaviour, so it lives there, not in a history record.
- **DEBUG shm** paths, env vars, or permissions change (`docs/reference/source-modules.md`; **monitor-debug-shm**).

New or moved pages follow **monitor-docs-structure-and-style** (placement, `EXTRA_DIST`, router, inbound links).

When the **monitor tarball / RPM version** changes, follow **monitor-version-and-packaging** (canonical `configure.ac` + `hpcperfstats.spec`) and update **HPCPerfStats/README.md** if it still cites an old `hpcperfstats-X.Y-Z...rpm` example.

This complements **global-testing-discipline** and **monitor-c-new-function-unittests** (tests) and **monitor-static-build-verification** (build path).
